{#- Names come from the devices themselves: escape what Markdown would read as a table, link or image. -#}
{%- macro md(v) -%}{{ (v ~ '') | replace('\\', '\\\\') | replace('|', '\\|') | replace('[', '\\[') | replace(']', '\\]') | replace('!', '\\!') | replace('<', '&lt;') | replace('>', '&gt;') | replace('`', '\\`') | replace('*', '\\*') | replace('_', '\\_') }}{%- endmacro -%}
{% set s = states.sensor | selectattr('entity_id', 'in', integration_entities('synology_srm_router'))
   | selectattr('attributes.rules', 'defined') | first %}
{% set rows = s.attributes.rules if s else [] %}
{% set to = {'input': 'router', 'forward': 'through', 'both_input_forward': 'router + through'} %}
| Rule | From → to | Ports | Hits |
|---|---|---|--:|
{% for r in rows -%}
| {{ '✅' if r.action == 'allow' else '⛔' }} {{ ('~~' ~ md(r.label) ~ '~~') if r.enabled == false else md(r.label) }} | {{ (r.in_interfaces | join(', ') ~ ': ') if r.in_interfaces }}{{ md(r.source_label or 'any') }} → {{ to.get(r.chain, r.chain) }}{{ (' ' ~ r.out_interfaces | join(', ')) if r.out_interfaces }}{{ (': ' ~ md(r.destination_label)) if r.destination_label }} | {{ md((r.ports or 'all') | replace(',', ', ') | truncate(32)) }} | {{ r.hits if r.hits is not none else '–' }}{{ '<br>⚠ duplicate' if r.duplicate }}{{ '<br>never hit' if r.enabled and r.hits == 0 and not r.duplicate }} |
{% endfor %}

✅ allow · ⛔ deny · ~~struck through~~: switched off · ⚠ duplicate: the same rule earlier in the list matches first · *router*: to the router itself, *through*: through it to another network. Hits count since SRM last built its firewall (after a change or a restart).
